---
/** ImbalanceTuning — safe imbalance treatment and nested tuning. */
---
<svg class="diagram-svg" viewBox="0 0 780 380" role="img" aria-label="A rare-positive dataset is split into training, validation, and test. Oversampling and class weights occur only inside each training fold. A threshold then chooses alerts from model scores. A tuning panel compares grid, random, and Bayesian search and notes that the test set remains locked. A warning states that synthetic examples must not cross into validation or test data.">
 <text x="390" y="31" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="27" fill="var(--ink)">balance the learning, protect the evaluation</text>
 <rect x="20" y="55" width="447" height="263" rx="14" fill="var(--paper-raise)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2"/>
 <text x="244" y="84" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="22" fill="var(--ink)">rare-positive pipeline</text>
 <rect x="48" y="108" width="196" height="54" rx="9" fill="var(--blueprint)" opacity=".84"/><text x="146" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="17" fill="var(--paper)">training fold only</text><text x="146" y="151" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--paper)">weights / SMOTE / pipeline</text>
 <path d="M245 135 H299" stroke="var(--ch1)" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#arr)"/><rect x="304" y="108" width="129" height="54" rx="9" fill="var(--highlight)" stroke="var(--ink)"/><text x="368" y="133" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="17" fill="var(--ink)">fit score</text><text x="368" y="151" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--ink-muted)">not a decision yet</text>
 <path d="M368 164 V205" stroke="var(--ch1)" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#arr)"/><line x1="86" y1="237" x2="405" y2="237" stroke="var(--ink-muted)" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="292" cy="237" r="12" fill="var(--highlight)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="91" y="219" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--ink-muted)">lower threshold</text><text x="405" y="219" text-anchor="end" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--ink-muted)">higher threshold</text><text x="245" y="282" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="17" fill="var(--alert)">select on validation · test once</text>
 <rect x="491" y="55" width="267" height="263" rx="14" fill="var(--paper-raise)" stroke="var(--ch2)" stroke-width="3"/>
 <text x="624" y="84" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="22" fill="var(--ink)">hyperparameter search</text>
 <text x="520" y="126" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="17" fill="var(--ink)">grid: planned combinations</text><text x="520" y="163" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="17" fill="var(--ink)">random: broad budgeted samples</text><text x="520" y="200" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="17" fill="var(--ink)">Bayesian: use prior trials</text><text x="520" y="237" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="17" fill="var(--ink)">Optuna: a library for search</text><text x="520" y="278" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--ink-muted)">same folds · same metric · fixed budget</text>
 <text x="390" y="355" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-hand)" font-size="17" fill="var(--alert)">never create synthetic rows before the split — they can leak into validation and test evidence</text>
 <defs><marker id="arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="7" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L8,3 z" fill="var(--ch1)"/></marker></defs>
</svg>
